      children: "Rate limiting patterns prevent abuse and spam. On Ethereum, you can use block timestamps to enforce cooldowns between user actions. On Solana, you might use account-level nonces or timestamp checks. On Sui, you can store timestamp in owned objects. The pattern involves tracking the last action time and requiring minimum intervals between operations. This prevents MEV bots from spamming transactions and protects against certain economic attacks."
    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.p, {
